            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0747" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11387: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-01T15:00:00+08:00">December 1, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—12:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>978. 1. We are confidentially informed by reliable competent source that German
                    Ambassador is expected here shortly to discuss Japanese peace proposals which
                    include Chinese (1) declaration of independence Outer [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Inner?</hi>] Mongolia, (2) participation in Anti-Comintern Pact, (3)
                    agreement to stop anti-Japanese propaganda, and on Japanese side resumption of
                        <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> in North China as regards Japanese
                    troops. I report this for what it may be worth. Our source states that it is
                    second definite Japanese attempt to initiate peace discussions and that these
                    proposals do not come from the Japanese military.</p>
                <p>2. My German colleague has told me in confidence that Japanese some time ago
                    asked Germany to propose to China that China initiate peace discussions but
                    German Government refused because the Japanese would not reveal what terms would
                    be acceptable to Japan.</p>
                <p>3. Repeated to Hankow, Shainghai, Peiping. Peiping please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
